# DocuTrust AI: Product Requirements Document

**Version:** 1.0 (build-ready draft)  |  **Date:** 31 October 2026  |  **Platform:** Web app, mobile-first and responsive

## 1. Product Overview

DocuTrust AI helps people and institutions answer two questions about important documents:

1. **Can I trust this document?** Upload a marks card, Aadhaar, PAN card, certificate or bank statement. Get a Trust Score, highlighted suspicious regions and a plain-language verification report in about 30 seconds.
2. **Do I understand what I am signing?** Upload a legal document. Get a simple summary, key clauses, risk flags and a translation into your own language, with audio and a chat to ask questions.

**Positioning:** DocuTrust AI is decision support, not legal proof. It flags evidence of editing and explains it. Final verification still rests with the issuing authority.

**Tagline options:** “Trust every document.” or “Verify. Understand. Decide.”

## 2. Problem Statement

- Editing software makes it easy to alter marks cards, Aadhaar cards, PAN cards, certificates and bank statements.
- Manual checking is slow, inconsistent and needs expertise, while colleges, banks, HR teams, government offices and law firms handle hundreds of documents a day.
- Legal documents are written in dense jargon. Most are in English, while many users read only a regional language, so people sign things they do not understand.

**Opportunity:** Combine image and PDF forensics, rule-based validation and AI language models in one calm, simple product that serves both the verifier and the ordinary citizen.

## 3. Goals, Non-Goals and Success Metrics

### Goals

- **G1.** Detect likely modifications in common Indian documents and explain them visually and in words.
- **G2.** Make legal documents understandable in simple language and in the user’s own language.
- **G3.** Deliver a minimalist, fast, trustworthy experience that a first-time user can use without instructions.
- **G4.** Offer an API so institutions can plug verification into their own workflows.

### Non-Goals (v1)

- Not a replacement for official portals (UIDAI, Income Tax/NSDL, DigiLocker, university verification).
- Not legal advice. No lawyer-client relationship is created.
- No face matching, liveness or full KYC.
- Full Aadhaar numbers are never stored.

### Success Metrics

| Metric | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Tamper detection recall on internal test set | 85% or higher at false-positive rate of 10% or lower |
| Time to first result (single-page image, p90) | 30 seconds or less |
| Legal summary time (20 pages, p90) | 45 seconds or less |
| First-time users completing a verification unaided | 90% or higher |
| Usability score (SUS) | 80 or higher |
| Summary helpfulness rating | 4.3 out of 5 or higher |
| Translations rated acceptable by native-speaker reviewers | 90% or higher |

