## 12. Scoring Logic

Initial weights (tune with test data):

| Module group | Weight |
| --- | --- |
| Pixel forensics | 30% |
| Field validation rules | 25% |
| Text and font consistency | 20% |
| Metadata and file structure | 15% |
| Layout and template match | 10% |

- Modules that do not apply (for example, template match on an unknown certificate) are dropped and weights renormalized.
- Confidence is derived from image quality, number of applicable modules and agreement between them.
- Hard-fail rules (FR-S3) override the weighted score.
- If confidence is Low and the score is mid-range, return **Inconclusive** with a request for a better scan or the original file.

## 13. Security, Privacy and Compliance

- Compliance with India’s **Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023**: explicit consent, purpose limitation, right to erasure, grievance contact.
- Follow UIDAI guidance: never store full Aadhaar numbers; mask by default; do not log them.
- Encrypt in transit (TLS 1.2 or higher) and at rest; per-file keys where feasible.
- Default retention is delete after analysis; background jobs purge expired files and verify deletion.
- Third-party APIs (OCR, LLM, speech) called only with the minimum content needed, under data-processing terms that disallow training on user data.
- No document content in logs or analytics. Access to stored files restricted and audited.
- Abuse prevention: rate limits, CAPTCHA for guests, malware scan on uploads, and guard against users using the tool to refine forgeries (do not reveal exact detection thresholds or pixel-level hints; show regions and reasons only).
- Clear disclaimers on every result and report.

## 14. Non-Functional Requirements

- **Performance:** Lighthouse performance 90 or higher on mobile; first contentful paint under 1.5 s on 4G.
- **Scalability:** horizontal worker scaling; queue depth alarms; 100 concurrent analyses at launch.
- **Reliability:** 99.5% uptime; retries for failed modules; partial results shown when one module fails.
- **Compatibility:** latest two versions of Chrome, Safari, Edge, Firefox; Android and iOS browsers.
- **Maintainability:** modular detectors behind a common interface so new checks can be added without touching the UI.
- **Explainability:** every score reproducible from stored module outputs.

## 15. Analytics

Privacy-respecting product analytics (no document content): activation (first result viewed), completion rate by step, drop-off on upload, share and report-download rate, language usage, summary helpfulness thumbs, false-positive and false-negative feedback buttons (“Was this result correct?”), time to result, error rates by module.

## 16. Testing and Datasets

- **Synthetic tamper set:** create genuine sample documents (your own and public sample templates, with fictional data), then tamper them by changing digits, swapping photos, pasting seals, editing PDFs, re-saving and screenshotting. Label ground truth.
- **Public research datasets** for image forensics benchmarking (for example CASIA, Columbia, CoMoFoD) to validate pixel modules.
- **Edge cases:** WhatsApp-compressed images, phone photos under poor light, scanned photocopies, rotated or cropped files, password-protected PDFs.
- **Legal summaries:** 50 sample agreements reviewed by a legal professional for accuracy; translation review by native speakers for each launch language.
- **Usability:** test with 10 or more users across age groups and languages before launch.
- **Quality gates:** no release if recall or false-positive targets are missed or if summaries cite non-existent clauses.

## 17. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| False positives or negatives harm trust | Confidence levels, Inconclusive state, clear limits, feedback loop, threshold tuning |
| Users treat results as legal proof | Disclaimers, “verify with issuer” next steps, report wording |
| LLM hallucination in legal summaries | Grounded extraction with clause references, strict schemas, refusal when unsure, human-reviewed test set |
| Translation errors on legal terms | Keep original term in brackets, glossary, native-speaker review, “report an error” button |
| Sensitive-data leakage | Minimal retention, masking, encryption, no logging of content |
| Forgers use the tool to improve fakes | Rate limits, coarse feedback, no exposure of internal thresholds |
| Template drift (new ID or marks card designs) | Template management in admin, periodic review |
| Low-quality uploads | On-device quality checks and retake guidance |

